# The fixes of the review of step 23, the budgets' part (finding 12): the
# workspace's files listed on the first `@` and kept compactly, and the
# coarse limit on a key's echo in the real binary. Broken one at a time,
# with the tests that must fail.

[break] the-files-listed-at-open
rule: The workspace's files are asked of the core on the first `@` typed, not when the session opens: an idle application holds no list of them.
file: crates/cortex-tui/src/app/state.rs
in: App::ask_files
find: && self.input.wants_files()
replace: && (self.input.wants_files() || self.session.is_some())
packages: cortex-tui
caught-by:
    app::tests::files::the_workspace_files_are_listed_on_the_first_at_and_not_when_the_session_opens

[break] the-files-asked-for-every-frame
rule: The workspace's files are asked for once: frames drawn while the list is on its way do not ask again.
file: crates/cortex-tui/src/app/state.rs
in: App::ask_files
find: self.files_listing = true;
replace: self.files_listing = false;
packages: cortex-tui
caught-by:
    app::tests::files::the_workspace_files_are_listed_on_the_first_at_and_not_when_the_session_opens
    app::tests::files::an_at_typed_before_the_session_is_open_lists_the_files_once_it_is

[break] a-candidate-starts-at-the-buffers-start
rule: Each candidate in the one buffer starts where the one before it ends.
file: crates/cortex-tui/src/complete/fuzzy.rs
in: Candidates::get
find: .map_or(0, |before| self.ends[before] as usize);
replace: .map_or(0, |_| 0);
packages: cortex-tui
caught-by:
    complete::fuzzy::tests::the_candidates_are_kept_in_one_buffer_in_order
    complete::fuzzy::tests::the_characters_in_order_ignoring_case_match

[break] a-path-not-ascii-matched-by-byte
rule: A candidate that is not ASCII is marked so, and matched by character.
file: crates/cortex-tui/src/complete/fuzzy.rs
in: Candidates::new
find: .push(if is_ascii { name } else { name | NOT_ASCII });
replace: .push(name);
packages: cortex-tui
caught-by:
    complete::fuzzy::tests::the_candidates_are_kept_in_one_buffer_in_order
    complete::fuzzy::tests::paths_that_are_not_ascii_match_by_character

[break] the-interface-waits-before-each-key
rule: A key reaches the screen of the real binary within the coarse limit: an interface thread that waits on something before taking a key fails a blocking test (review of step 23, finding 12d).
file: crates/cortex-tui/src/app.rs
in: run_with
find: input |= take(terminal, presenter, &mut scheduler, app, &event)?;
replace: input |= { std::thread::sleep(std::time::Duration::from_millis(600)); take(terminal, presenter, &mut scheduler, app, &event)? };
packages: cortex-cli
caught-by:
    cortex-cli::system tui::sys_a_turn_with_tools_runs_in_the_interface_and_the_terminal_is_put_back
